# Alert 3 – High Memory Utilization

## Alert

```text
Memory Utilization : 89%
Threshold : 88%
```

---

## Investigation

Verified memory utilization.

```bash
free -h
top & press 'm'
vmstat 1 5
```

Checked processes consuming memory.

```bash
ps -eo pid,user,%mem,cmd --sort=-%mem | head
```

Determined whether memory usage was due to:

* Application memory leak
* Memory exhaustion
* Linux page cache

---

## Root Cause

Depending on the workload, memory utilization was caused by one of the following:

* Application memory leak
* High application workload
* Linux page cache consuming available memory

---

## Resolution

If application memory leak was suspected:

* Raised a case with the Application and Operations teams.
* Shared process memory statistics.

If cache usage was responsible and maintenance was approved:

```bash
sync
echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches
```

Cache was cleared only during maintenance or off-peak hours.

If memory was genuinely insufficient, planned a memory upgrade after analysing workload trends.

---

## Skills Demonstrated

* Linux Memory Analysis
* Memory Leak Investigation
* Capacity Planning

